# SpeakesQuery is a local-trust desktop app - there is no auth layer (no
# SECRET_KEY, no admin login, no API tokens).  All settings below are
# optional; the only common reason to populate this file is SMTP for email
# delivery of scheduled-search alerts.  Everything else is set in-app on
# the Settings page or via global_settings.yaml.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Precedence - why every line below is commented out by default
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both the Docker image (via `env_file:` in desktop_app/docker-compose.yml)
# and PyCharm's default Python run config load this file into the
# process environment at startup.  Env vars WIN over values saved on
# the Settings page - so if you uncomment a line here, it will override
# whatever you configure in the UI.  For most users the right choice is
# to leave every SMTP_* line commented out and configure email through
# Settings → Email instead; that way the UI is the single source of
# truth and `.env` stays out of the auth path entirely.
#
# Known placeholder values (`you@gmail.com`, `your_16_char_app_password`,
# etc.) are auto-detected and ignored with a one-shot WARN line - so a
# stock `.env` copied verbatim by install.sh cannot silently poison
# AUTH even if someone forgets to edit it.  Real credentials pasted in
# place of the placeholders are used normally.

# ── Email / SMTP (optional - leave commented out to use Settings page) ──
# For Gmail: use an App Password (https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords)
# Uncomment AND replace the placeholder values to use env-var config:
#
# SMTP_USER=you@gmail.com
# SMTP_PASSWORD=your_16_char_app_password
# SMTP_SERVER=smtp.gmail.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_FROM=              # defaults to SMTP_USER
# SMTP_STARTTLS=true      # set to false for port 465 (implicit SSL)

# ── Anthropic Claude API (optional, for the analyzer + alert groups) ──
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ── Allowed API domains for sandboxed ingestion scripts (optional) ──
# Comma-separated regex patterns.  When unset, the per-task setting from
# global_settings.yaml's `allowed_api_domains` is used instead.
# ALLOWED_API_DOMAINS=^api\.example\.com$,^data\.example\.com$
